{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_tower_log_convexity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lepton_tower_log_convexity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_tower_bend_invariant","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.not_two_positive_modes_of_bend_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.not_two_positive_modes_of_bend_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_tower_log_convexity.lean#L131-L143","doc":"**Contrapositive — the form the screen is actually used in.**\n\nA tower whose measured bend exceeds `1` is not a positive combination of two\ngeometric modes, whatever the coefficients and rates.  Applied to the charged\nleptons (`bend ≈ 12.295`), this excludes the additive-interface shape without\nany appeal to how extreme a fitted parameter would have to be. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bend_le_one_of_two_positive_modes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bend_le_one_of_two_positive_modes","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_tower_log_convexity.lean#L112-L129","doc":"**Hence the bend of a positive two-mode tower is at most `1`.**\n\nStated in the same `bend` currency as the multiplicative screen so the two\nresults compose: the observed lepton bend is `≈ 12.295`, and this says the\nadditive class cannot exceed `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.twoMode_log_convex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.twoMode_log_convex","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_tower_log_convexity.lean#L86-L110","doc":"**A positive two-mode tower is log-convex.**\n\n`x(w) = c·g^w + d·h^w` with `c, d ≥ 0` and `g, h > 0` satisfies\n`x(w+2)² ≤ x(w)·x(w+4)`.\n\nThe proof is the Lagrange form of Cauchy–Schwarz: the deficit is the perfect\nsquare `c·d·g^w·h^w·(g² − h²)²`, so it is not merely non-negative but\n*strictly* positive unless the two rates coincide or a coefficient vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}